1837:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c **** /** @defgroup TIM_Group3 Input Capture management functions
1838:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****  *  @brief    Input Capture management functions 
1839:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****  *
1840:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c **** @verbatim   
1841:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****  ===============================================================================
1842:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****                   ##### Input Capture management functions #####
1843:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****  ===============================================================================  
1844:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****          
1845:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****             ##### TIM Driver: how to use it in Input Capture Mode #####
1846:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****  ===============================================================================
1847:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****     [..]    
1848:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****     To use the Timer in Input Capture mode, the following steps are mandatory:
1849:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****        
1850:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Enable TIM clock using RCC_APBxPeriphClockCmd(RCC_APBxPeriph_TIMx, ENABLE) 
1851:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           function
1852:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****        
1853:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Configure the TIM pins by configuring the corresponding GPIO pins
1854:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****        
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc0EAqnP.s 			page 34


1855:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Configure the Time base unit as described in the first part of this driver,
1856:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           if needed, else the Timer will run with the default configuration:
1857:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) Autoreload value = 0xFFFF
1858:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) Prescaler value = 0x0000
1859:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) Counter mode = Up counting
1860:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) Clock Division = TIM_CKD_DIV1
1861:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           
1862:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Fill the TIM_ICInitStruct with the desired parameters including:
1863:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) TIM Channel: TIM_Channel
1864:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) TIM Input Capture polarity: TIM_ICPolarity
1865:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) TIM Input Capture selection: TIM_ICSelection
1866:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) TIM Input Capture Prescaler: TIM_ICPrescaler
1867:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****         (++) TIM Input Capture filter value: TIM_ICFilter
1868:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****        
1869:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Call TIM_ICInit(TIMx, &TIM_ICInitStruct) to configure the desired channel 
1870:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           with the corresponding configuration and to measure only frequency 
1871:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           or duty cycle of the input signal, or, Call TIM_PWMIConfig(TIMx, &TIM_ICInitStruct) 
1872:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           to configure the desired channels with the corresponding configuration 
1873:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           and to measure the frequency and the duty cycle of the input signal
1874:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           
1875:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Enable the NVIC or the DMA to read the measured frequency. 
1876:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           
1877:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Enable the corresponding interrupt (or DMA request) to read the Captured 
1878:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           value, using the function TIM_ITConfig(TIMx, TIM_IT_CCx) 
1879:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           (or TIM_DMA_Cmd(TIMx, TIM_DMA_CCx)) 
1880:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****        
1881:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Call the TIM_Cmd(ENABLE) function to enable the TIM counter.
1882:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****        
1883:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       (#) Use TIM_GetCapturex(TIMx); to read the captured value.
1884:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****        
1885:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****       -@- All other functions can be used separately to modify, if needed,
1886:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****           a specific feature of the Timer. 
1887:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c **** 
1888:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c **** @endverbatim
1889:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****   * @{
1890:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_tim.c ****   */
